  "tagline": "Apache TinkerPop's reference server for running Gremlin traversals over any compatible graph.",
  "description": "Apache TinkerPop is the vendor-neutral graph computing framework behind the Gremlin traversal language, and Gremlin Server is its reference server that exposes any TinkerPop-enabled graph over WebSocket or HTTP. Out of the box it hosts TinkerGraph, an in-memory reference graph that is handy for tests, prototyping and small analytical jobs; providers such as JanusGraph and HugeGraph embed Gremlin Server, and Neptune and Aerospike Graph implement its protocol. The 3.8 line is current (3.8.2 in September 2026), with 4.0 in beta. It is infrastructure more than a database: there is no durable storage engine by default.",
